---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
const updated = '25 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What data Data Governance Signal processes about visitors and readers, and why.">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p>A portal about data governance should practise what it covers. Here is exactly what we process and why.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>In short</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No cookies, no advertising trackers, no profiling.</li>
        <li>Visitor statistics are aggregated and do not identify you.</li>
        <li>We only hold your email address if you write to us or subscribe to the newsletter.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        Data Governance Signal is the controller for the processing described here. Contact:
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
      <p>
        The site is delivered by Cloudflare, which processes technical data such as your IP address and browser details to
        serve pages and protect the site against attacks. This is necessary to run the site (legitimate interest, Article
        6(1)(f) GDPR).
      </p>
      <p>
        We measure visits with <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>. It does not set cookies, does not use local
        storage and does not build profiles of individuals. We see only aggregated figures such as page views, referring
        sites, countries and device types. We use them to understand which content is useful (legitimate interest).
      </p>

      <h2>Writing to us</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us, we use your address and message only to reply and to handle your request, for example a
        correction. We keep the correspondence as long as needed for that purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to The Monday Signal, your email address is stored by our newsletter service,
        <strong>Buttondown</strong> (a US-based provider), and used only to send you the newsletter. Subscription is
        double opt-in: nothing is sent until you confirm by email. Every email has an unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing
        removes you from the list. We have switched off open and click tracking, we do not sell or share subscriber
        addresses, and we do not combine them with other data. The legal basis is your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR),
        which you can withdraw at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>If the portal changes owner</h2>
      <p>
        If Data Governance Signal is transferred to a new owner, for example through a sale, subscriber addresses and the
        data described here pass to the new owner, who must continue to use them only as this notice describes. We will
        tell subscribers before the transfer, and you can unsubscribe at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to sources</h2>
      <p>
        Articles link to original sources on other websites. Those sites have their own privacy practices, which we do not
        control.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask for access to, correction or deletion of personal data we hold about you, object to processing based
        on legitimate interest, or lodge a complaint with a data protection authority. Write to
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: calc(var(--measure) + 2 * var(--gutter));
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }
  .updated {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
</style>
